    "title": "Fall festival at Blue Skies Facility delights high-needs youth - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christopher Walker ,\n6 hours ago\nWICHITA FALLS ( KFDX/KJTL ) — Some high-needs youth in the Texoma area got a chance to break away from their norm and experience a little Halloween fun.\nOn Wednesday, October 22, Blue Skies Residential Facility hosted a fall festival for its youth in care. Fun projects like face painting, slime making, and other craft projects were available.\nMany of the youth come from trauma and behavioral issues and need a safe, structured place to receive therapeutic help. Texas Family Initiative director of marketing, Kara-Kae James, said the annual event is like a field trip and allows for the kids to experience the holidays the same way many kids do.\n“We love these kids so much, and we want them to feel just normal. We want them to feel like any other kid and have this kind of love and attention. And so, in any way we can do that.”\nJames said programs like this rely on donations, and with the holidays just around the corner, they need help from the community to provide Christmas for these kids. If you would like to help, click here .",
